submit for consideration; as, to raise a point of order; to raise an objection. ; To cause to rise, as by the effect of leaven; to make light and spongy, as bread. ; To cause (the land or any other object) to seem higher by drawing nearer to it; as, to raise Sandy Hook light. ; To let go; as in the command, Raise tacks and sheets, i. e., Let go tacks and sheets. ; To create or constitute; as, to raise a use, that is, to create it.	o:5wn,79,4;ere,53,5;so7,46,4;2bpd,31,14~2bpd,31,14;ere,53,5;so7,46,4;5wn,79,4	s:1i5v,23,2~1i5v,23,2	d:23hz,13,13;2hq,12,3;14yr,8,11~23hz,13,13;14yr,8,11;2hq,12,3
